ct-displayed-integer","capture_precision":"collection-run-start","selection_policy":"latest-known-snapshot; minimum on same-time conflict"},"text_status":"captured_displayed_source_text","text_source":"https://nitter.jaydenha.uk/AOC/with_replies?cursor=DAAHCgABHVwYZMm__pYLAAIAAAATMjAwNzgzODA3NTA2Njc1MzI5MAgAAwAAAAIAAA","text_truncated":false},{"id":"x-1990867231006470406","post_id":"1990867231006470406","platform":"x","author":"AOC","original_url":"https://x.com/AOC/status/1990867231006470406","published_at":"2025-11-18T19:38:31.053Z","published_date":"2025-11-18","date_precision":"millisecond","source_ids":["nitter-public-timeline"],"text":"This is how I feel about it.\n\nI loathe machine politics and got to office defeating an incumbent who got in that way.\n\nHowever there are quite a few problems with choosing to grind the entire House to a halt to force all 435 members across the country to do a rushed vote on this one individual instance (of many, mind you!).\n\n1. Why is it that this objection wasn’t brought up until now? The author had no problem when Bill Posey did it, or even earlier this year when a member’s account was tweeting post mortem for an election. The standard of this resolution is unevenly applied and choosing to enforce it via privileged resolution for some but not others does open legitimate questions of rationale or motivation. Why not care about this for them, but care about it now? This question has not b…","post_kind":"quote","is_repost":false,"author_verified":true,"like_count":3779,"likes_captured_at":"2026-10-28T23:51:54.990547+00:00","likes_source":{"provider":"nitter-public-timeline","url":"https://nitter.jaydenha.uk/AOC/with_replies?cursor=DAAHCgABHVwYZMm__pYLAAIAAAATMjAwNzgzODA3NTA2Njc1MzI5MAgAAwAAAAIAAA","sha256":"bf7c2c7766cc44bdeea38bbb0cb95aacd3fe06a3b2cfce3254d65be1d73592bb","count_precision":"exact-displayed-integer","capture_precision":"collection-run-start","selection_policy":"latest-known-snapshot; minimum on same-time con